<section>
<h2>1. Project Overview</h2>
<p><strong>Project Name:</strong> TextBook Swap SA – Second-Hand Textbook Swap</p>
<p><strong>Module:</strong> PRP372S – Project Presentation 3</p>
<p><strong>Institution:</strong> Cape Peninsula University of Technology (CPUT)</p>
<p><strong>Project Type:</strong> Entrepreneurial WIL Project</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>2. Project Purpose</h2>
<p>TextBook Swap SA aims to help CPUT students reduce the cost of textbooks by providing a platform where students can buy and sell second-hand textbooks. The project encourages affordable access to academic resources and the reuse of learning materials.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>3. Project Vision</h2>
<p>To create a reliable, accessible and student-friendly platform that makes second-hand textbooks more affordable and helps students share academic resources.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>4. Project Objectives</h2>
<ul>
<li>Develop a functional platform for second-hand textbook listings.</li>
<li>Help students find textbooks relevant to their studies.</li>
<li>Support affordable buying and selling between students.</li>
<li>Provide a user-friendly experience across desktop and mobile devices.</li>
<li>Encourage the reuse of textbooks and reduce unnecessary spending.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section>
<h2>5. Team Roles and Responsibilities</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Litha Owethu Mazibuko – Project Facilitator/Scrum Master:</strong> Facilitates team communication, supports Agile practices and monitors sprint progress.</li>
<li><strong>Samkelo Mahlangu – Product Owner/Content Lead:</strong> Prioritises the product backlog and helps ensure the platform meets user needs.</li>
<li><strong>Coben Maistry – Frontend Developer:</strong> Contributes to the user interface and search functionality.</li>
<li><strong>Angelia Van der Westhuizen – UI/UX and QA Lead:</strong> Focuses on usability, interface design and testing across devices.</li>
<li><strong>Ongeziwe Raqa – Deployment and Documentation Lead:</strong> Supports deployment, repository management and project documentation.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section>
<h2>6. Team Values</h2>
<p>The team values respect, communication, teamwork, transparency, constructive feedback and continuous improvement.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>7. Communication Plan</h2>
<p>The team uses WhatsApp for regular updates, virtual check-ins and meetings to discuss progress and challenges. GitHub supports version control and collaboration.</p>
</section>

<section>
<h2>8. Project Goals</h2>
<p>The project aims to provide a functional textbook-swapping platform with a clear interface, textbook listings and search functionality. The team also aims to test the website on different devices and improve the platform based on feedback.</p>
</section>

